        "title": "Apple will stream the next Formula 1 Grand Prix free for everyone",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/18/apple-will-stream-the-next-formula-1-grand-prix-free-for-everyone/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/apple-tv-f1-grand-prix-austrai.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1558\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The next Formula 1 race will stream completely for free on the <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/getappletvplus\">Apple TV app</a> in the United States, no subscription required.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most races this year require an <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/getappletvplus\">Apple TV subscription</a> to view, but when the deal was announced, Apple said that select races will be in front of the paywall altogether. The Austrian Grand Prix (June 26 – June 28) is the first time they are delivering on that promise.</p>",
