        "title": "Siri AI hints at new iPhone 18 Pro design change",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/16/siri-ai-hints-at-new-iphone-18-pro-design-change/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/siri-ai-27-dark.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Siri AI is available now in the iOS 27 beta after you <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/08/ios-27-beta-1-has-a-waitlist-for-accessing-new-siri-ai/\" type=\"post\" id=\"1055603\">get off the waitlist</a>, and it includes a not-so-subtle hint about a design change that’s rumored for this fall’s <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/04/iphone-18-pro-six-new-features-are-coming-later-this-year/\" type=\"post\" id=\"1033425\">iPhone 18 Pro</a>.</p>",
